## 3. Suites and gates

Gate descriptors live in `.gates/<family>/*.gates`. They are YAML descriptors,
not scripts: for manual work, read the descriptor and run the `command` it
declares from its `cwd` (the repo root when it declares none).

| gate | descriptor | runs | about |
|---|---|---|---|
| `build` | `.gates/Berreman/build.gates` | `dotnet build Berreman.slnx -c Release` from `Berreman/` | 2 min |
| `unit-tests` | `.gates/Berreman/unit-tests.gates` | `BerremanTests` from its folder | **~30 min whole** — run by class |
| `constructor-unit-tests` | `.gates/OpticalConstructor/constructor-unit-tests.gates` | `OpticalConstructor.Tests` | < 1 min |
| `ui-smoke` | `.gates/OpticalConstructor/ui-smoke.gates` | `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, trait `Category=ui-smoke` | < 1 min |
| `ui-tests` | `.gates/OpticalConstructor/ui-tests.gates` | `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, not `ui-smoke` | ~3 min |
| `elevation` | `.gates/Elevation/elevation.gates` | `Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1 -ExcludeRules ELEV004` from the repo root | ~4 min |
| `elevation-full` | `.gates/Elevation/elevation-full.gates` | the same with `-All` | ~4 min, can be silent for long |

- Tests run on **Microsoft.Testing.Platform** with xUnit v3, after the build:
  `dotnet test --no-build -c Release` from the test project's folder.
- **Filters are xUnit v3's own**: `--filter-class`, `--filter-method`,
  `--filter-trait`, `--filter-not-trait`. One class with its theory rows:
  `--filter-method "<Ns>.<Class>.*" --filter-method "<Ns>.<Class>"`. Never VSTest's
  `--filter`.
- The gates read the MTP summary (`Test run summary: Passed!`, `succeeded: N`).
  A count never regresses.
- **The ELEV gates read the working tree.** The scoped `elevation` gate analyzes
  every product project that compiles a changed `.fs` (git status, untracked
  included) plus every project that references it, so run it **before** the
  commit. A finding recorded in `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json` does not
  fail; a new one does, and **so does a recorded one that is gone** — a fix deletes
  or lowers its entry in the same change. `ELEV-GATE: OK` is green.
- The analyzers' rule configuration is `.elevation-analyzers.json`. **Never edit it,
  never edit the analyzers, never add an entry to the known-findings list, never
  re-record it.** ELEV004 is excluded in the command, not in the rules.
- Out of the ELEV scope by the analyzers' own configuration: the test projects and
  the vendored `MathNetNumerics/`.

### 3.1 Known flakes

None is recorded. A test that fails once is re-run once before it is called red.

