## 6. Walls

- **STL (`C:/GitHub/Softellect`) and ASG (`C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator`)
  are read-only from this repository.** Read them freely as the model; never
  edit, build, pack or bump them. STL's documents disagreeing with the analyzers
  is not ours to fix (spec 0048 `.manual/002` R6).
- **`MathNetNumerics/`** is a vendored, customized MathNet.Numerics built from
  source and referenced as projects. It is outside the ELEV scope; do not edit
  it, and never replace it with the NuGet package.
- **`BerremanRunner/` and `BerremanModelGenerator/`** are stale and not in
  `Berreman.slnx`. They are not elevated and not touched.
- **Never touch `*.nb` files** (Mathematica, binary), nor the `.docx` files at
  the root.
- **One `.fsproj` per folder.** Share sources by `<Compile Include … Link=… />`.
- **No new comments in `.fsproj` / `.csproj`.**
- **There are no deferrals.** Nothing is staged, held back, or promised to a
  later spec. Work that cannot be finished is escalated, never postponed.
- **LF is King.** `core.autocrlf` is `false`; `.gitattributes` stores text as
  LF. Check `git diff --numstat` against `--ignore-cr-at-eol` after editing. When
  appending, match the **blob's** endings.
- **F# discipline is binding on every change**, per `AGENTS.md`: elevate every
  primitive, `camelCase` values and record fields, a space before every colon,
  `{` on its own line, interpolated strings never `sprintf`, pattern-match rather
  than `.Value` / `.IsSome`, errors as `Result` values, explicit concrete types on
  public signatures, unique names (no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]` to dodge a
  collision).
- **Git is forward-only.** No `checkout` / `reset` / `rebase` / `amend` /
  `revert` / `stash`. To recover a file, `git show <ref>:<path>`.
- **Keep `.ps1` files ASCII** outside `<# #>` blocks.
- **No build step, gate, test or fixture may depend on a OneDrive folder**
  (`AGENTS.md`, operator ruling 2026-11-01).

